        GALAXY is a war game for two players,  written at the
        Tel Aviv university CS lab. It's manual page gives a brief
        introduction. The main point is that *BOTH* players give
        their commands at the same time from different terminals.
        It is ever interesting, for the opponent is another shrewd
        brain.
     
        Mail me if you want the sources. There are about 7500 source
        lines.
        If enough requests will arrive, I'll post it all.
     
NAME
     galaxy - A two player duel in space
     
DESCRIPTION
     Galaxy is a game of strategy and cunning for two players. It
     is played on two different CRT terminals. The game displays
     a map of a remote part of the universe, with two identical
     galaxies on each terminal.  Each player owns one galaxy.
     The aim of the game is to conquer the opponent's Capital,
     which is the center of his galaxy.
     Both players give commands simultaneously, without knowing
     the enemy's position and intentions.
     There are quite a few commands, that enable each player to
     perform various tasks. The Galaxy's document contains
     specifications and examples. The "help" command enables online
     review of major parts from that document.
     
